    narr:narration """On 2026-08-26, DaveQuantum announced a storage-layer replacement for the analytics pipeline: [switching from PostgreSQL to QuantumDB](narr:Expr_1E2EQuantum1787736270121_1), framed as a decided change performed as fact rather than proposed. The rationale rests on two legs — [10x query performance and lower licensing cost](narr:Expr_1E2EQuantum1787736270121_2) — and the broader narrative positions this as a [replacement, not an extension](narr:Narrative_DatabaseMigrationDecision) of the existing storage layer. The decision is restated in parallel summary bullets: [database migration arrow](narr:Expr_1E2EQuantum1787736270121_3), [performance gain](narr:Expr_1E2EQuantum1787736270121_4), and a committed [Q3 2026 timeline](narr:Expr_1E2EQuantum1787736270121_5). A second broader narrative frames [performance and cost as the stated case](narr:Narrative_InfrastructureCostPerformanceRationale) for infrastructure change, raising the question of whether those claims narrow or hold as the migration proceeds. All children share a single date and a single speaker; the style runs parallelism across the summary bullets, and the conviction pattern splits between decision-level assertions (the switch, the timeline) and claim-level justifications (the performance and cost numbers).""" ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1E2EQuantum1787736270121_1> ;
